{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1578649732,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzNTYxNzQ2NQ=="},"target":"77e27696acf565da0ca1521004625f93cc6524db6f21db5a0f82f0d48764209c","message":"(basically, this issue restates #1284)\n\nDesired behavior: I want to automatically ``publish`` all branches of a dataset with `datalad publish` to a remote, instead of only the master and git-annex branch.\n\nTo do this, I configured the remote in question in ``.git/config`` with ``git config --local remote.\u003cremote-name\u003e.push 'refs/heads/*' ``.\n\nA ``git push [\u003cremote-name\u003e]`` pushes all branches, as requested. ``datalad publish --to \u003csibling-name\u003e`` does not care about this configuration, and only pushes master and git-annex. Specifying the configuration in the call itself via ``datalad -c 'remote.public.push=refs/heads/*' publish --to public`` does not push any more branches as well.\n\nThe culprit is in here: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/a1554a95fbcd07254bc3faaa797133039f237272/datalad/distribution/publish.py#L462","files":null}]}